---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'About';
const description = 'About NovelTest - Fastest Way To Write Your Novel';
const permalink = `${Astro.site.href}about`;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} permalink={permalink} current="about">
  <div class="container">
     <h1>About</h1>
     <h2>Official Statement & Stance On AI</h2>

     <p>Because of the way the world is now and because you may wonder about the use of AI on this site and in my books, I think it's important to make an official statement about my use of AI.</p>
     <ol>
        <li> None of this site or my books have been written by AI.</li>
        <li> I wrote every word that you read on this site and in my books.</li>
        <li> I do use AI, but I use it like a search engine, not as a replacement for my brain.</li>
        <li> I also verify that the things AI tells me are correct, because (as I'm sure you know) it often hallucinates (makes things up).</li>
        <li> AI writing is bland and boring. It has no gut. AI has no feelings and doesn't understand what it means to have feelings and that blandness comes through when it communicates.</li>
     </ol>

        <h3>AI Slop Explained</h3>
        <p>
Imagine ideas as all the food of the world thrown into a giant blender and whipped until it's a juice.  Imagine drinking that mess.  You may imagine it tastes like everything but in reality It would taste like nothing.  That's what AI writing is like.
        </p>
        <h3> Writing For Humans, By A Human</h3>
        <p>I'm a human and I wrote the articles on this site and my book's for myself and for others who still want to think for themselves and connect as humans.</p>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-image {
    float: right;
    margin: -3em -7em 2em 2em;
    max-width: 300px;
  }

  .about-image img {
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 1.5em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1020px) {
    .about-image {
      float: none;
      margin: 0 auto 2em;
    }
  }
</style>
